id: pm-wrdctq
title: Expose explicit paired sampling for core-only telemetry reads
description: Deliver the reusable explicit sampling primitive underneath the automatic-volume issue. A configured inclusion probability and no-extensions boundary retain or drop successful lifecycle pairs together; errors remain probability one. This task does not claim automatic default-loop suppression.
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-12T22:13:12.976Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T22:24:55.158Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-12T22:24:27.336Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-12T22:24:27.336Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Configured core-only reads retain or drop full successful pairs with an inclusion probability; mutations and failures remain unsampled; invalid probabilities are refused by fallback to full retention; documentation states default and interruption limitations.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make read telemetry volume explicitly controllable with unbiased pair weights
value: Reusable safe telemetry primitive for core-only agents and SDK consumers
parent: pm-um3teu
resolution: PM_TELEMETRY_READ_SAMPLE_RATE selects complete successful lifecycle pairs only with the no-extensions boundary; retained pairs carry their inclusion probability and failures retain probability one.
expected_result: A reusable explicit control safely reduces configured core-only reads without sampling writes or losing failure pairs.
actual_result: Probability validation and retained dropped failure pair tests pass in the linked run and 8789-test full-source suite with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Defaults remain unsampled and interruption limits are documented.
